# M24.2b -- run RTEMS's own `ticker` sample, built for zynqmp_rpu_lock_step with the
# container-built toolchain (third_party/rtems-container/output), on Renode's mainline Zynq
# UltraScale+ Cortex-R5 platform, on rpu0 only, same platform/reset convention as hello.resc.
# Adapted from the read-only host reference third_party/rtems/run-renode/ticker.resc (only
# the source ELF differs). `ticker` exercises the clock driver (M24's stated reason this
# sample "matters more than hello" -- M24.3/M24.4 depend on the clock driver working), unlike
# `hello` which explicitly disables it.
#
# Expected output, stated before running (from testsuites/samples/ticker/ticker.scn, the
# sample's own reference transcript, and tasks.c/init.c's logic: clock set to 09:00:00
# 12/31/1988; TA1/TA2/TA3 wake every 5/10/15s respectively and print the time; the test exits
# once a task observes second >= 35):
#   *** CLOCK TICK TEST ***
#   TA1 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:00   12/31/1988
#   TA2 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:00   12/31/1988
#   TA3 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:00   12/31/1988
#   TA1 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:05   12/31/1988
#   TA1 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:10   12/31/1988
#   TA2 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:10   12/31/1988
#   TA1 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:15   12/31/1988
#   TA3 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:15   12/31/1988
#   TA1 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:20   12/31/1988
#   TA2 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:20   12/31/1988
#   TA1 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:25   12/31/1988
#   TA1 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:30   12/31/1988
#   TA2 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:30   12/31/1988
#   TA3 - clock_get_tod - 09:00:30   12/31/1988
#   *** END OF CLOCK TICK TEST ***
#
# The test needs >=35s of simulated time to reach its own exit condition; 60s of virtual
# RunFor is used for margin (not tuned to the minimum -- this is slack, not a tolerance).

:name: zynqmp-rpu-lockstep-ticker

using sysbus
using sysbus.cluster0
using sysbus.cluster1

mach create "zynqmp-rpu-ticker"

machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/zynqmp.repl

# NOTE (bug found and fixed in this task, see REPORT.md and hello.resc's comment for the
# full root-cause): `@$ORIGIN/...` suppresses `$ORIGIN` substitution (the `@` marks a
# literal string), so Renode failed to create a file literally named `$ORIGIN/...` and
# aborted the script before `quit`, hanging Renode forever. Dropped the `@` so `$ORIGIN`
# substitutes correctly, consistent with the `LoadELF $ORIGIN/...` line below.
uart0 CreateFileBackend $ORIGIN/ticker_uart.log true

macro reset
"""
    cluster0 ForEach IsHalted true
    cluster1 ForEach IsHalted true
    rpu0 IsHalted false

    sysbus LoadELF $ORIGIN/ticker.exe cpu=rpu0
"""

runMacro $reset
